  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Pipeline & Backdoor is the most famous wave on the planet, a heaving barrel that detonates over an uneven lava-slab reef only about 80 metres off Ehukai Beach Park on Oahu's North Shore. It's really two waves sharing one peak: Pipeline, the legendary left, and Backdoor, the super-hollow right that funnels across the shallow reef toward Off-The-Wall. Outer reefs refract and focus arriving swell onto the inside reef, so a wave that looks absent on a flat day can come roaring back to life when the right swell shows up. It's rated among the best waves in the world. Skill (surfnerd): Expert. Surf-forecast Pipeline_1: \"Pipeline in Oahu is an exposed reef break that has fairly consistent surf, although summer tends to be mostly flat. The best wind direction is from the southeast. Most of the surf here comes from groundswells and the best swell direction is from the west northwest. Often Crowded. Watch out for rocks and locals.\" Surf-forecast Backdoor-5: \"Backdoor in Oahu is an exposed reef break that has quite reliable surf, although summer tends to be mostly flat. Works best in offshore winds from the southeast. Clean groundswells prevail and the ideal swell angle is from the northwest. A popular wave that can get growded. Watch out for - Rocks.\" Surf-forecast Banzai-Pipelines-and-Backdoor: \"Banzai Pipelines and Backdoor in Oahu is an exposed reef break that has quite reliable surf, although summer tends to be mostly flat. Offshore winds are from the east southeast. Groundswells more frequent than windswells and the best swell direction is from the northwest. R"
