  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Haleiwa is a powerful right-hand reef break on the North Shore, and the town behind it is the area's commercial hub as well as a proving ground for many of Hawaii's best surfers, past and present. The wave breaks over an uneven reef off Ali'i Beach Park. On a small day the broken peaks can look easy and inviting, but that first impression is deceptive. Surfnerd lists this break twice (haleiwa, haleiwa-hawaii); merged, same facing. Second Surfnerd entry https://www.surfnerd.com/surf-forecast/haleiwa-hawaii: workable swell WNW - NNW , offshore None, 6ft - 15ft, Lava, Coral, Reef, Right, Left, Low, Mid, High, Beginner, Intermediate, Expert, Autumn, Winter, Spring, Shortboard, Bodyboard. Skill (surfnerd): Intermediate. Surf-forecast Haleiwa-Toilet-Bowl: \"Haleiwa/Toilet Bowl in Oahu is an exposed reef break that has pretty consitent surf, although summer tends to be mostly flat. The best wind direction is from the southeast. Groundswells more frequent than windswells and the ideal swell direction is from the northwest. There is a right breaking reef. When the surf is up, crowds are likely Watch out for rips, sharks and rocks.\" Wannasurf haleiwa: quality Regional Classic; experience Experienced surfers; wave Reef-rocky, Right and left; swell size Starts working at 1.0m-1.5m / 3ft-5ft and holds up to 4m+ / 12ft; crowd weekday Crowded, weekend Crowded. Access (surfnerd): Facilities are well covered here, with restrooms, showers, a lifeguard, a surf school, and a surf shop. Parking includes a car park with free parking, along with paid and roadside options. Other "
