  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Velzyland, better known as V-Land, is an excellent right-hand reef break on Oahu's North Shore, named after the California surfer and shaper Dale Velzy. It sits in a big bay just beyond Backyards, in the shadow of Phantom Reef, which focuses incoming swell into the bay and funnels it onto V-Land's shallow, uneven lava ledge. On a good day it throws bowling, hollow rights with rippable walls and a square inside barrel section. Shorter lefts are on offer too, though there is no paddle channel to get you back outside. Skill (surfnerd): Expert. Surf-forecast Velzy-Land: \"Velzy Land in Oahu is an exposed reef break that has very consistent surf, although summer tends to be mostly flat. Offshore winds are from the south southeast. Groundswells more frequent than windswells and the ideal swell angle is from the northwest. Reef breaks provide lefts and rights. A fairly popluar wave that can sometimes get crowded Hazards include rocks and locals.\" Wannasurf velzy_land: quality World Class; experience Experienced surfers; wave Reef-rocky, Right; swell size Starts working at Less than 1m / 3ft and holds up to 2m+ / 6ft+; crowd weekday Few surfers, weekend Crowded. Access (surfnerd): Park on Kam Highway, walk through the gates, and head north up the beach. Lock your car before you paddle out. Other guide pins from this position: surf-forecast Velzy-Land 1.7 km, wannasurf velzy_land 0.2 km."
