  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Rocky Point is a flat, curving reef on the North Shore, roughly 250 yards wide and one of the most consistent waves on the coast. It breaks both left and right, serving up everything from soft walls to clean barrels and punchy air sections. The setup splits into two broad zones known as Rocky Rights and Rocky Lefts, each holding several takeoff points that come alive in different conditions. Skill (surfnerd): Intermediate. Surf-forecast Rocky-Point_1: \"Rocky Point in Oahu is an exposed reef break that has very reliable surf, although summer tends to be mostly flat. Ideal winds are from the south southeast. Tends to receive distant groundswells and the best swell direction is from the northwest. There are left and right breaking reefs. When the surf is up, crowds are likely Take care of rocks and locals.\" Access (surfnerd): Reach it by driving about half a mile past Ehukai Beach Park on Kamehameha Highway, then turning onto Ke Nui Road and parking where authorized. Public access paths lead down to the sand, and there's a car park nearby. Other guide pins from this position: surf-forecast Rocky-Point_1 1.3 km."
