  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Laniakea, known locally as Lani's, is a broad right-breaking reef about two and a half miles north of Haleiwa on Oahu's North Shore. The main takeoff sits roughly 400 yards offshore, over one half of a massive lava hammerhead; the other half forms the left known as Jocko's, a quarter-mile to the northeast. A channel running out beside the point cuts partway through the reef, giving a fast paddler a way across the thinnest section between closeouts. On its day it ranks among the North Shore's finest waves, a long ride that offers a bit of everything. Check: surfnerd states facing NW but best swell NE (90 degrees apart); both are as published. Skill (surfnerd): Intermediate. Surf-forecast Laniakea-Reef-and-Holtons: \"Laniakea Reef and Holtons in Oahu is an exposed reef break that has consistent surf, although summer tends to be mostly flat. Works best in offshore winds from the southeast. Most of the surf here comes from groundswells and the ideal swell direction is from the northwest. A reef breaks right. Sometimes crowded. Hazards include rocks and sharks.\" Wannasurf laneakea: quality Regional Classic; experience All surfers; wave Reef-rocky, Right and left; swell size Starts working at Less than 1m / 3ft and holds up to 5m / 16 ft and over; crowd weekday Crowded, weekend Crowded. Access (surfnerd): Getting in is easy. Park in the dirt lot on the inland side of Kam Highway, just across from Laniakea beach. Other guide pins from this position: surf-forecast Laniakea-Reef-and-Holtons 1.2 km, wannasurf laneakea 0.2 km."
