  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Chun's is a right-hand reef break on Oahu's North Shore, tucked between Jocko's and Waimea Bay. It breaks over uneven, often shallow and sharp reef across an elbow, throwing up both a left and a right. The right is faster but shorter and draws very shallow on the inside, while the bonus left off the middle runs shoulderier and more forgiving as it spills into deeper water. Its three sections, the outside, middle, and bowl, each offer roll-ins, workable walls, and the odd tube, and it can turn hollow and fast when it's on. Skill (surfnerd): Beginner. Surf-forecast Chuns-Reef: \"Chuns Reef in Oahu is an exposed reef break that has very reliable surf, although summer tends to be mostly flat. Works best in offshore winds from the southeast. Most of the surf here comes from groundswells and the ideal swell angle is from the north. The quality of the surf isn't affected by the tide. Likely to be crowded if working. Hazards include - Rocks.\" Surf-forecast Chuns-and-Jocks-Reefs: \"Chuns and Jocks Reefs in Oahu is an exposed reef break that is usually a safe bet, although summer tends to be mostly flat. Offshore winds blow from the east southeast. Tends to receive distant groundswells and the best swell direction is from the northwest. Both left and right reef breaks. The quality of the surf isn't affected by the tide. Likely to be crowded if working. Hazards include rocks/rips.\" Wannasurf chuns_reef: quality Regional Classic; experience Experienced surfers; wave Reef-rocky, Right and left; swell size Starts working at Less than 1m / 3ft and holds up to 2m+ / 6ft+; "
