  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Jocko's is a left reef pointbreak on the North Shore, named after local legend Jock Sutherland. Compared to its higher-profile neighbors, it hands you a relatively easy takeoff and long rides, but there's real substance here. When a big WNW-NW swell fills in, Jocko's turns into a proper, heavy left barrel. Skill (surfnerd): Intermediate. Surf-forecast Jockos-Point: \"Jockos Point in Oahu is an exposed point break that has fairly consistent surf, although summer tends to be mostly flat. Ideal winds are from the southeast. Most of the surf here comes from groundswells and the best swell direction is from the north northwest. Good surf at all stages of the tide. An uncrowded break, even when it is working. Beware of - Rips / undertow - Rocks - Sharks.\" Wannasurf Jockos_Point: quality World Class; experience Pros or kamikaze only...; wave Point-break, Left; swell size Starts working at 2m-2.5m / 6ft-8ft and holds up to 5m / 16 ft and over; crowd weekday Few surfers, weekend Few surfers. Access (surfnerd): Jocko's is easy to reach, with a car park offering free parking plus roadside parking where authorized. There are showers on hand for after your session. Other guide pins from this position: surf-forecast Jockos-Point 0.2 km, wannasurf Jockos_Point 0.3 km."
