  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Hultin's is a right-hander that breaks well outside Laniakea, sitting just west of the top of Jocko's and east of the regular Laniakea takeoff zone. On northerly angled swells it links up with Laniakea proper, essentially a further-out takeoff on the same stretch of North Shore reef. The wave peels right over a bottom of lava, rock, and coral, and getting out there means a very long paddle both ways. Skill (surfnerd): Intermediate, Expert. Access (surfnerd): Park in the dirt lot on the inland side of Kam Highway, just across from Laniakea beach. From there it's a long paddle out to the peak and back. surfnerd pin 0.0 km from ours."
