  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Puaena Point, also known as Puni's, is a reef break that peels into the Haleiwa boat channel, which shelters it from unruly north swells and gusty northeast trades. The rights are the main event, breaking over an uneven reef before drifting into the deep channel. Surfnerd has 2 entries for this break with different stated facings (puaena-point=W, puaena-point-hawaii=WNW); seaward uses the primary entry (puaena-point), both kept. Second Surfnerd entry https://www.surfnerd.com/surf-forecast/puaena-point-hawaii: workable swell NW - N , offshore None, 5ft - 15ft, Lava, Rock, Coral, Reef, Point, Right, Low, Mid, High, Beginner, Intermediate, Expert, Autumn, Winter, Spring, Shortboard, Funboard, Longboard, Fish, Bodyboard, Gun, Tow. Skill (surfnerd): Intermediate. Surf-forecast Puaena-Point: \"Puaena Point in Oahu is an exposed reef break that only works when conditions are just right. Summer in particular tends to be flat. Works best in offshore winds from the southeast. Groundswells more frequent than windswells and the best swell direction is from the northwest. A reef breaks right. Often Crowded. Beware of urchins, rocks and pollution.\" Wannasurf puaena_point: quality Normal; experience All surfers; wave Reef-coral, Right and left; swell size Starts working at 2m-2.5m / 6ft-8ft and holds up to; crowd weekday Crowded, weekend Ultra crowded. Access (surfnerd): There's a car park at the spot, along with restrooms, showers, and camping. Other guide pins from this position: surf-forecast Puaena-Point 0.4 km, wannasurf puaena_point 0.1 km, surfnerd puaena-point-ha wannasurf pin 0.1 km from ours. surfnerd pin 0.0 km from ours. surf-forecast pin 0.4 km from ours (its coordinates are given to 0.01°). surf-forecast: \"exposed reef\"."
