  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Backyards is a wide, exposed reef flanking Sunset, where scattergun peaks stalk an uneven bottom that breaks both left and right. The shallow, urchin-covered reef adds to the heaviness, and this is a spot happy to hand out a beating to anyone who paddles out. Outside Backyards sits far enough off the beach to suck in more ocean swell than Waimea, and when it turns on, 50ft-plus faces are on the cards. Skill (surfnerd): Expert. Surf-forecast Backyards_1: \"Backyards in Oahu is an exposed reef break that has very consistent surf, although summer tends to be mostly flat. Works best in offshore winds from the south southeast. Most of the surf here comes from groundswells and the ideal swell angle is from the northwest. There are left and right breaking reefs. Unlikely to be too crowded, even when the surf is up. Hazards include rocks and locals.\" Access (surfnerd): There is a car park nearby. Other guide pins from this position: surf-forecast Backyards_1 0.9 km."
