  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Chambers is a fast, hollow reef break tucked between Rocky Point and Pupukea on Oahu's North Shore. It breaks over a shallow reef with some pockets of sand, in clean, clear blue water. The lefts are the main draw here, though the rights come to life too when the swell lines up. Skill (surfnerd): Intermediate, Expert. Surf-forecast Rocky-Rights-Lefts-Gas-Chambers: \"Rocky Rights/Lefts and Gas Chambers in Oahu is an exposed beach and reef break that has very consistent surf, although summer tends to be mostly flat. Ideal winds are from the south southeast. Most of the surf here comes from groundswells and the ideal swell angle is from the northwest. There are left and right breaking reefs. Sometimes crowded. Take care of rocks in the line up.\" Access (surfnerd): Drive about half a mile past Ehukai Beach Park on Kam Highway, then pull onto Ke Nui Road and park where authorized. From there, take the public access streets and trails down to the beach. Other guide pins from this position: surf-forecast Rocky-Rights-Lefts-Gas-Chambers 0.9 km."
