  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Ehukai is a reef break along the Pupukea stretch, breaking over an uneven lava shelf and sand. On smaller days it throws up mellow reef peaks that offer some respite from the heavier surf nearby, and when the sand banks up just right the lefts and rights turn hollow and genuinely epic. This same stretch holds the shallow, spitting pits of Gas Chambers. Skill (surfnerd): Intermediate. Surf-forecast Ehukai-Gums: \"Ehukai/Gums in Oahu is an exposed beach and reef break that has reasonably consistent surf, although summer tends to be mostly flat. Offshore winds blow from the east southeast. Tends to receive distant groundswells and the best swell direction is from the northwest. Waves at the beach are mainly lefts and there is left hand reef break too.. Surfable at all stages of the tide. It's often crowded here. Beware of rips and rocks.\" Wannasurf ehukai: quality Regional Classic; experience All surfers; wave Sand-bar, Right and left; swell size Starts working at 1.0m-1.5m / 3ft-5ft and holds up to 2.5m+ / 8ft+; crowd weekday Crowded, weekend Ultra crowded. Access (surfnerd): You'll find all the amenities of Ehukai Beach Park here, including restrooms, showers and a lifeguard. There's a car park with free parking, plus roadside parking. Other guide pins from this position: surf-forecast Ehukai-Gums 1.8 km, wannasurf ehukai 0.0 km."
