  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Rockpile sits between Log Cabins and Off-The-Wall, breaking right in front of the pile of rocks that gives it its name. It's a big, powerful left running over uneven reef, and it can be tricky to catch at its best. When it's on, though, it throws a powerful big-wave face that can barrel. Skill (surfnerd): Expert. Surf-forecast Rockpiles-Logcabins: \"Rockpiles/Logcabins in Oahu is an exposed reef break that has fairly consistent surf, although summer tends to be mostly flat. Offshore winds blow from the east southeast. Tends to receive distant groundswells and the ideal swell direction is from the northwest. There are left and right breaking reefs. It very rarely gets crowded here. Beware of rips and rocks.\" Access (surfnerd): There's a lifeguard on hand, and you can use the car park with free parking or find roadside parking along the highway where authorized. Other guide pins from this position: surf-forecast Rockpiles-Logcabins 2.3 km."
