  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Off-The-Wall, also known as Kodak Reef, is a reef break sitting just west of Backdoor and Pipeline. It breaks over an uneven slab of reef as a wedging right, with smaller lefts peeling back toward Backdoor. On the right wave it throws a clean, almond-shaped barrel, running hollow and fast when it's on. This is an expert-only wave, and the rides tend to be short and punchy rather than long. Skill (surfnerd): Expert. Surf-forecast Offthe-Wall-Insanities: \"Off the Wall/Insanities in Oahu is an exposed reef break that has quite reliable surf, although summer tends to be mostly flat. Offshore winds are from the east. Tends to receive distant groundswells and the ideal swell direction is from the northwest. Reef breaks provide lefts and rights. Best around mid tide. It's often crowded here. Hazards include urchins, rips and rocks.\" Wannasurf off_the_wall: quality World Class; experience Experienced surfers; wave Reef-rocky, Right and left; swell size Starts working at Less than 1m / 3ft and holds up to 2m+ / 6ft+; crowd weekday Crowded, weekend Crowded; page has no GPS position. Access (surfnerd): There's a lifeguard on hand, and parking is free. Use the Ehukai Beach Park lot, or park along Kam Highway where authorized. Other guide pins from this position: surf-forecast Offthe-Wall-Insanities 1.8 km."
