  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Turtle Bay West is a mellow reef break on the eastern edge of Kawela Bay, with the right peeling in the shadow of the Turtle Bay Resort. It handles both rights and lefts over a reef of lava and coral, and the water here is clean and strikingly clear. Once a quiet escape from the North Shore crush, it has become a genuine winter hotspot, and while it stays mellow by North Shore standards, it can turn really good when the swell and wind line up. Don't confuse it with Turtle Bay East, which sits around the peninsula on the resort's east side. Skill (surfnerd): Beginner, Intermediate, Expert. Access (surfnerd): Parking is easy and close to the break. wannasurf pin 0.4 km from ours. surfnerd pin 0.1 km from ours. surf-forecast pin 1.5 km from ours (its coordinates are given to 0.01°). surf-forecast: \"exposed beach and reef\"."
