  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: South Shore - Ala Moana Park isn't a single break but a cluster of good reef waves packed into about a half-mile of coast. From east to west you'll find Kaisers, Rockpiles, Ala Moana Bowls, and Magic Island, each with its own character, from rights and lefts to barrels and bowls. The reef serves up consistently fun surf across all of them, so you can pick the peak that suits your session. Skill (surfnerd): Intermediate, Expert. Access (surfnerd): You can reach any of the spots from the breakwater and channels, or paddle straight out from the small beach beside the Ala Moana parking lot across the shallow reef platform, which gets a little sketchy at low tide. The paddles to and from the beach can be long, but it eases off once you're outside. Keep in mind the reef is shallow and sharp, and the nearby harbor means pollution is a factor, especially after heavy rain. surfnerd pin 0.1 km from ours."
