  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Kaisers is the easternmost break on the Ala Moana reef, a steep, fast, bowly right that peels over a shallow live-coral bottom. It throws a good barrel section off the peak and is fun to backdoor, and because the right spills into a channel you get an easy paddle back out. There is also a left, usually a little more slopey, that tends to close out on the inside. It is an expert-level reef break, and when everything lines up it is one of the better waves in the area. Skill (surfnerd): Expert. Surf-forecast Kaisers: \"Kaisers in Oahu is an exposed reef break that has dependable surf. Summer offers the favoured conditions for surfing. Ideal winds are from the north. Windswells and groundswells in equal measure and the best swell direction is from the south southeast. The reef provides both left and right breaks. Good surf at all stages of the tide. Sometimes crowded. Watch out for rocks, obstacles, locals and sharks.\" Wannasurf kaisers: quality Regional Classic; experience Experienced surfers; wave Reef-coral, Right and left; swell size Starts working at Less than 1m / 3ft and holds up to 2.5m+ / 8ft+; crowd weekday Few surfers, weekend Ultra crowded. Access (surfnerd): There is plenty on hand nearby, including restrooms, showers, a lifeguard, a surf school, and a surf shop. Parking is paid, metered, or roadside with a car park available, and it can get tricky around the harbour. To get out, walk the east breakwater by the Ala Moana parking lot to the end and paddle out through the channel, or paddle from the little beach near the parking lot across the reef "
