  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Kewalo's is a consistent reef break that fires a hollow, bad-tempered left over dead coral. It barrels, sections, and shuts down with unpredictable regularity, shifting around the lineup and keeping everyone on their toes. The rights can barrel as well, but they quickly run into shallow close-outs. Across the channel sits Point Panic, a metronomic right tube favored by the bodysurf and fin set, who ride close to the rock seawall. Skill (surfnerd): Expert. Surf-forecast Kewalos: \"Kewalos in Oahu is an exposed reef break that has reliable surf. Summer offers the best conditions for surfing. The best wind direction is from the north. Tends to receive a mix of groundswells and windswells and the best swell direction is from the south southeast. Both left and right reef breaks. Good surf at all stages of the tide. When the surf is up, crowds are likely Take care of Man-made danger (buoys etc...) and sharks.\" Wannasurf kewala_basin: quality Normal; experience Experienced surfers; wave Reef-coral, Right and left; swell size Starts working at Less than 1m / 3ft and holds up to 3m+ / 10ft+; crowd weekday Crowded, weekend Ultra crowded. Access (surfnerd): There's no beach here, so paddle out from the wall. You'll find restrooms and showers, and parking runs the gamut from a car park with free parking to paid, metered, roadside, and restricted spots. Keep in mind the coral heads by the channel, the heavy fishing-boat traffic, some pollution, and sharks that are often spotted in the area. Other guide pins from this position: surf-forecast Kewalos 0.4 km, wannasurf ke"
