  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Sand Island is a State Recreation Area fronted by a brilliant white ribbon of sand, tucked behind the warehouses and shipyards of the industrial island. The setup is a mish-mash of reefy peaks breaking over dead coral, with both lefts and rights on offer. Most of the action happens at the east end near the tower, where waves can break outside and reform closer in. Despite sitting so near town, it is often one of the best places to beat the crowds, almost hidden in plain sight. It is only average most of the time, but it can turn genuinely fun. Skill (surfnerd): Beginner. Wannasurf Sand_Island: quality Normal; experience All surfers; wave Reef-rocky, Right and left; swell size Starts working at Less than 1m / 3ft and holds up to 3m+ / 10ft+; crowd weekday Empty, weekend Few surfers. Access (surfnerd): Getting in is easy at Sand Island State Recreation Area, which has a car park with free parking. You will also find restrooms, showers, and camping on hand. Other guide pins from this position: wannasurf Sand_Island 0.1 km. wannasurf pin 0.1 km from ours. surfnerd pin 0.0 km from ours."
