  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Populars, or Pop's, is a long, curving stretch of reef in Waikiki, sitting just west of Canoes and a bit further out. It's a peak with a decent right that peels and swings down the line, throwing up a few bowly sections toward the inside, alongside a shorter, mushier left. Most days it's a mellow, user-friendly wave, but it can really come alive when a solid swell is running. The bottom is dead coral reef, so keep that in mind. Skill (surfnerd): Intermediate. Surf-forecast Populars: \"Populars in Oahu is an exposed reef break that usually has waves. Summer offers the best conditions for surfing. Offshore winds blow from the north. Tends to receive a mix of groundswells and windswells and the ideal swell direction is from the south southeast. There is a right hand reef break. The quality of the surf isn't affected by the tide. Likely to be crowded if working. Beware of rocks, obstacles, locals and sharks.\" Access (surfnerd): Populars is easy to reach, sitting right in front of the Sheraton Waikiki Hotel, across the channel and east of Canoes. You'll find restrooms, showers, a lifeguard, plus a surf school and surf shop nearby. Parking options include a car park along with metered, roadside, and other paid and restricted spaces. The paddle out from the beach is long, but it's manageable once you're outside. Other guide pins from this position: surf-forecast Populars 0.7 km."
