  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Three's and Four's are a pair of right-hand reef breaks in Waikiki that share a stretch of live coral reef. Three's is usually the pick of the two: it turns on with clean, racy righthanders that can barrel through some hollow sections before running into a deep channel at the wave's end, which makes for an easy paddle back to the lineup. Four's, just along the reef, is more sectiony and offers some easier lefts peeling toward Kaisers. Skill (surfnerd): Intermediate. Surf-forecast Number-Threes: \"Number Threes in Oahu is an exposed reef break that usually has waves. Summer offers the optimum conditions for surfing. Offshore winds blow from the north. Most of the surf here comes from groundswells and the optimum swell angle is from the south southeast. Reef breaks provide lefts and rights. Good surf at all stages of the tide. Often Crowded. Take care of rocks, obstacles, locals and sharks.\" Surf-forecast Number-Fours: \"Number Fours in Oahu is an exposed reef break that has reasonably consistent surf. Summer offers the favoured conditions for surfing. Offshore winds blow from the north. Most of the surf here comes from groundswells and the best swell direction is from the south southeast. A choice of left and right reefs. Good surf at all stages of the tide. When the surf is up, it can get quite busy in the water. Take care of rocks, obstacles, locals and sharks.\" Wannasurf threes: quality Regional Classic; experience Experienced surfers; wave Reef-coral, Right and left; swell size Starts working at 1.5m-2m /5ft-6ft and holds up to 2.5m+ / 8ft+; crowd weekda"
