  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Queen's sits right in the heart of Waikiki, a reef break that peels over lava, rock, and coral. On small to medium days a single A-frame peak splits fairly evenly into a fun but shorter left and a longer right. When a bigger swell fills in, it reshapes into a long left, one of the best on the South Shore, backed by a shorter right. It can barrel on occasion, but most of the time you get an easy, rippable face. Skill (surfnerd): Intermediate, Expert. Surf-forecast Queens_1: \"Queens in Oahu is an exposed beach and reef break that has quite reliable surf. Summer offers the favoured conditions for surfing. Offshore winds blow from the north northeast with some shelter here from east winds. Tends to receive a mix of groundswells and windswells and the best swell direction is from the south southeast. Reef breaks provide lefts and rights. The quality of the surf isn't affected by the tide. Beware of .\" Wannasurf queens: quality World Class; experience All surfers; wave Reef-coral, Right and left; swell size Starts working at 1.0m-1.5m / 3ft-5ft and holds up to 2.5m+ / 8ft+; crowd weekday Ultra crowded, weekend Ultra crowded. Access (surfnerd): Getting in is easy, with parking in or near Kuhio Beach Park. The paddle out and back to the beach is long, but it settles down once you are out in the lineup. Other guide pins from this position: surf-forecast Queens_1 0.2 km, wannasurf queens 0.1 km."
