  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Tonggs is a coral reef break with both lefts and rights, sitting just off Kalakaua. The lefts are improver-friendly, throwing the odd hollow section as they double up over the uneven coral, while the right runs faster before closing out. The left eventually fades into a deeper channel. It's a consistent spot, so there's usually something on offer when the swell is running. Skill (surfnerd): Beginner. Wannasurf tongg_s: quality Normal; experience All surfers; wave Reef-coral, Right and left; swell size Starts working at Less than 1m / 3ft and holds up to 1m+ / 3ft+; crowd weekday Crowded, weekend Ultra crowded; page has no GPS position. Access (surfnerd): Paddle out from the tiny beach off Kalakaua. There are showers on hand, and parking comes in free, paid, metered, and roadside options, though the metered spots nearby can be hard to come by. wannasurf page https://www.wannasurf.com/spot/North_America/USA/Hawaii/Oahu/tongg_s/index.html had no coordinates; not used. surfnerd pin 0.0 km from ours."
