  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Cliffs sits below the Diamond Head Rd lookouts, a scattering of five or six reefs and channels that throw long, rippable walls both left and right over dead coral. It's often the biggest spot on the South shore, and with so many peaks spread along the reef it soaks up plenty of surfers and kites without funnelling everyone onto a single takeoff. Skill (surfnerd): Intermediate. Surf-forecast Cliffs_1: \"Cliffs in Oahu is an exposed beach and reef break that usually has waves. Summer offers the optimum conditions for surfing. The best wind direction is from the north. Most of the surf here comes from groundswells and the best swell direction is from the south. Both left and right reef breaks. When the surf is up, it can get quite busy in the water. Take care of rocks,etc.\" Wannasurf cliffs: quality Normal; experience All surfers; wave Reef-coral, Right and left; swell size Starts working at Less than 1m / 3ft and holds up to 2.5m+ / 8ft+; crowd weekday Crowded, weekend Ultra crowded. Access (surfnerd): There's a car park with free parking plus roadside parking, and showers to rinse off after your session. Other guide pins from this position: surf-forecast Cliffs_1 0.6 km, wannasurf cliffs 0.1 km."
