  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Black Point is a left reefbreak that peels off the top of the point at Kaiko's, near Ka'alawai Beach on Oahu. It isn't a true point, though: left and right peaks are scattered along the reef, so a good swell throws up everything from barrel sections and corners to ramps and open faces. The bottom is a mix of lava, rock, and coral. Skill (surfnerd): Intermediate, Expert. Access (surfnerd): There are two ways out. The short option is off the rocks, which gets tricky on a sizeable swell. The easier route is to enter from the beach, though that means a long paddle out and around to the point. surfnerd pin 0.1 km from ours."
