  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Ewa Beach Park is a long, southeast-facing stretch of sandbar and reefbreaks on Oahu. It sits among the military suburbs of Iroquois Point, near the entrance to Pearl Harbor, where you'll also find appropriately named breaks like Marine Beach and Tank Traps. Skill (surfnerd): Beginner. Surf-forecast Ewa-Beach-Park: \"Ewa Beach Park in Oahu is an exposed reef break that has quite reliable surf and can work at any time of the year. The best wind direction is from the north northwest. Groundswells and windswells are equally likely and the ideal swell direction is from the south southeast. Reef breaks provide lefts and rights. It's sometimes crowded here. Watch out for rocks.\" Access (surfnerd): There's a car park with free parking plus roadside parking, and the beach is backed up by restrooms, showers, and a lifeguard. Other guide pins from this position: surf-forecast Ewa-Beach-Park 1.3 km."
