  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: White Plains Beach is one of the best places to learn on the island, right up there with Waikiki. Fun, friendly peaks roll in and constantly reform, running left or right across a flat, dead coral shelf that often has a nice dusting of sand over it. It's a super-wide playing field, with room for swarms of shortboarders, bodyboarders, and especially longboarders spread across the width and breadth of the lineup. Skill (surfnerd): Beginner. Surf-forecast White-Plains-Beach: \"White Plains Beach in Oahu is an exposed reef break that has reliable surf and can work at any time of the year. Works best in offshore winds from the north. Windswells and groundswells in equal measure and the best swell direction is from the south. Both left and right reef breaks. It's often crowded here. Beware of rocks/sharks.\" Wannasurf white_plains_beach: quality Sloppy; experience All surfers; wave Reef-coral, Right and left; swell size Starts working at Less than 1m / 3ft and holds up to 2m+ / 6ft+; crowd weekday Crowded, weekend Ultra crowded. Access (surfnerd): A massive car park with free parking plus roadside parking keeps things easy, and the lot fills up with families drawn to the facilities. You'll find restrooms, showers, a lifeguard, a surf school, and a surf shop, along with shops, shady picnic spots, and BBQ pits. Other guide pins from this position: surf-forecast White-Plains-Beach 1.6 km, wannasurf white_plains_beach 0.4 km."
