  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Barbers Point is a coral reef setup in Kalaeloa, near the Campbell industrial park. A point wave breaks directly out beyond the lighthouse, but the real draw is the variety of peaks spread down the beach, which shift with the swell direction. The bottom is dead coral studded with rocky outcrops, so where you choose to paddle out matters. Because the spot sits in such an exposed position, wind is often the deciding factor. Check: surfnerd states facing SSW but best swell W (67.5 degrees apart); both are as published. Skill (surfnerd): Intermediate. Surf-forecast Barbers-Point-Coast-Guard-Jetty: \"Barber's Point - Coast Guard Jetty in Oahu is an exposed reef break that has fairly consistent surf and can work at any time of the year. Offshore winds are from the north. Windswells and groundswells in equal measure and the optimum swell angle is from the south. A choice of left and right reefs. The quality of the surf isn't affected by the tide. Even when there are waves, it's not likley to be crowded. Beware of sharks,.\" Wannasurf barber_s_point_-_coast_guard_jetty: quality Regional Classic; experience Experienced surfers; wave Reef-coral, Right and left; swell size Starts working at 1.0m-1.5m / 3ft-5ft and holds up to 2m+ / 6ft+; crowd weekday Empty, weekend Few surfers. Access (surfnerd): You will find it at Barbers Point Beach Park, with a car park offering free parking plus roadside parking. Facilities include restrooms, showers, camping, and a lifeguard. Take care with the reef and rocky entry and exit points, and be aware that big tiger sharks are known h wannasurf page is 3.5 km from our pin (over 3 km); not used. surfnerd pin 0.0 km from ours. surf-forecast pin 0.6 km from ours (its coordinates are given to 0.01°). surfnerd swell exposure \"E - NW\" is the half-circle centred on its facing; its break notes and workable swell support swell from that side. surf-forecast: \"exposed reef\"."
