  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Tracks is a long reef with a sandy inside in Kahe Beach Park, breaking over dead coral close to the shore. It throws both lefts and rights: the lefts show up on south to southwest swells, while punchy rights fire on north to northwest swells. The main peak sits down near the power plant, producing electric rights and longer lefts, and a handful of lesser peaks stretch north toward Nanakuli. With everything breaking so close in, it is also a great spot to watch the action. Skill (surfnerd): Beginner. Surf-forecast Nanakuli-Tracks: \"Nanakuli Tracks in Oahu is an exposed reef break that has unreliable waves with no particular seasonal pattern. Works best in offshore winds from the east northeast. Most of the surf here comes from groundswells and the optimum swell angle is from the southwest. Good surf at all stages of the tide. The location means that it never gets crowded. Watch out for - Urchins - Rocks - Localism - Sharks.\" Surf-forecast Tracks-Nanakuli: \"Tracks(Nanakuli) in Oahu is an exposed beach and reef break that has consistent surf and can work at any time of the year. Offshore winds are from the northeast. Groundswells more frequent than windswells and the ideal swell angle is from the west. A choice of left and right reefs. Sometimes crowded. Take care of sharks,.\" Wannasurf nanakuli_tracks: quality Normal; experience All surfers; wave Reef-coral, Right and left; swell size Starts working at 2m-2.5m / 6ft-8ft and holds up to 2.5m+ / 8ft+; crowd weekday Few surfers, weekend Few surfers. Access (surfnerd): There is a car park with free parking righ"
