  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Kahuku, also known as 7th Hole, sits off the 7th hole of the Kahuku Golf Course at the start of the Windward Side, just around the bend from the North Shore. It's a reef break that offers both a powerful left and right, split by a deep channel that's often sharky. When a solid northeast swell lines up with offshore winds from a passing front, it's one of the best spots on the Windward Side, with long rides and barrels, though catching it that good isn't all that common. Skill (surfnerd): Beginner, Intermediate, Expert. Access (surfnerd): Cross the golf course at or near the 7th hole to reach the break. It's a long paddle out, though you get to use the channel, and the long rides mean long paddles back. When the spot's working, you'll figure out the way easily enough. surfnerd pin 0.0 km from ours."
