  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Makapu'u is arguably Oahu's best bodysurf and bodyboard spot, known for long, trundling lefts that end in a huge shorebreak barrel. It breaks over uneven reef and sand and throws both lefts and rights. The Beach Park enforces a no-surfboards policy, which the lifeguards police, but stand-ups are allowed to take on the heavy, barreling right that peels over the lava shelf at Makapu'u Point, in front of Sea Life Park. Surfnerd lists this break twice (makapuu, makapuu-hawaii); merged, same facing. Second Surfnerd entry https://www.surfnerd.com/surf-forecast/makapuu-hawaii: workable swell NNE - E , offshore None, 4ft - 8ft, Lava, Rock, Coral, Sand, Beach, Reef, Point, Right, Left, Low, Mid, High, Intermediate, Expert, Autumn, Winter, Spring, Summer, Shortboard, Bodyboard, Skimming, Bodysurfing. Skill (surfnerd): Beginner. Surf-forecast Makapu: \"Makapu'u in Oahu is an exposed beach break that has fairly consistent surf and can work at any time of the year. The best wind direction is from the west southwest. Windswells and groundswells in equal measure and the ideal swell direction is from the east southeast. The beach break provides left and right handers. Sometimes crowded. Watch out for rocks/crowds.\" Wannasurf makapuu: quality Normal; experience Experienced surfers; wave None, Right and left; swell size Starts working at Less than 1m / 3ft and holds up to 2.5m+ / 8ft+; crowd weekday Few surfers, weekend Crowded. Wannasurf Makapuu_Beach: quality World Class; experience All surfers; wave Beach-break, Right and left; swell size Starts working at Less than 1m /"
