  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Hookipa is a cluster of quality reefbreaks on Maui's north-central coast, working both left and right over uneven reef. It sits at the heart of Hawai'i's wind and kitesurfing scene, but on calm mornings the peaks belong to surfers. The break splits into several distinct spots spread along Ho'okipa Beach Park: Pavilions, Middles, the Point, and Lane. Skill (surfnerd): Intermediate. Surf-forecast Hookipa: \"Hookipa (Ho'okipa) in Maui is an exposed reef break that has fairly consistent surf. Winter is the optimum time of year for surfing at Ho'okipa. Offshore winds are from the south. Clean groundswells prevail and the best swell direction is from the north northeast. There are left and right breaking reefs. Surfable at all stages of the tide. It's sometimes crowded here. Watch out for urchins, rips, rocks, locals and sharks.\" Wannasurf hookipa: quality Regional Classic; experience All surfers; wave Point-break, Right; swell size Starts working at Less than 1m / 3ft and holds up to 5m / 16 ft and over; crowd weekday Few surfers, weekend Few surfers. Wannasurf hookipa_beach: quality Regional Classic; experience Experienced surfers; wave Reef-coral, Right and left; swell size Starts working at 1.5m-2m /5ft-6ft and holds up to 4m+ / 12ft; crowd weekday Few surfers, weekend Crowded. Access (surfnerd): Access is easy, with paid parking in car parks right at the break. There are restrooms, showers, and a lifeguard on hand, and you can enter the water from various points along Ho'okipa Beach Park. Other guide pins from this position: surf-forecast Hookipa 1.4 km, wa"
