  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Pavilions is a right-hand reef break that runs down the eastern point, tucked out of the wind and walling up beautifully into a defined channel. That channel makes the paddle back out easy, and the wave has a fun, ripable feel that keeps people coming back. Skill (surfnerd): Intermediate. Surf-forecast Pavillions: \"Pavillions in Maui is an exposed reef break that has consistent surf. Winter is the best time of year for surfing here. The best wind direction is from the south. Most of the surf here comes from groundswells and the best swell direction is from the north northeast. A left hand reef break. Good surf at all stages of the tide. A fairly popluar wave that can sometimes get crowded Watch out for urchins, rips, rocks, locals and sharks.\" Access (surfnerd): There's a car park with both free and paid parking, plus extra spaces up on the lookout. Facilities include restrooms, showers, and a lifeguard on hand. Other guide pins from this position: surf-forecast Pavillions 1.7 km."
