  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Kanaha is a consistent right-hand reef break at the start of Maui's wind corridor, on a north-facing stretch of coast near the airport. The wind that funnels through here draws kite and windsurfers, and the outside reefs usually throw up messy, wild peaks. When kona winds blow, both Kanaha and the better reefs up at Sprecklesville can clean up into picture-perfect left and right walls with the odd tube. Surfnerd lists this break twice (kanaha, kanaha-hawaii); merged, same facing. Second Surfnerd entry https://www.surfnerd.com/surf-forecast/kanaha-hawaii: workable swell NW - ENE , offshore None, 3ft - 10ft, Lava, Rock, Coral, Reef, Right, Left, Low, Mid, High, Beginner, Intermediate, Autumn, Winter, Spring, Shortboard, Funboard, Longboard, Fish, Bodyboard, Kiteboard. Skill (surfnerd): Intermediate. Surf-forecast Kanaha: \"Kanaha in Maui is an exposed reef break that has quite reliable surf. Winter is the best time of year for surfing here. Works best in offshore winds from the southeast. Most of the surf here comes from groundswells and the best swell direction is from the north northeast. Good surf at all stages of the tide. A fairly popluar wave that can sometimes get crowded Watch out for - Sharks.\" Wannasurf Kanaha: quality Regional Classic; experience All surfers; wave Reef-coral, Right and left; swell size Starts working at 1.0m-1.5m / 3ft-5ft and holds up to 3m+ / 10ft+; crowd weekday Few surfers, weekend Crowded. Other guide pins from this position: surf-forecast Kanaha 0.7 km, wannasurf Kanaha 1.2 km, surfnerd kanaha-hawaii 0.9 km."
