  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Waiehu sits in the built-up area of Kahului, where a few basic boulder beach peaks break close to town. The real draw is just to the south, where a brace of heavy, localised reefs fire over uneven reef. Water quality in this part of the coast is not great. Skill (surfnerd): Expert. Surf-forecast Waiehubeachpark: \"Waiehu beach park in Maui is an exposed reef and point break that has reliable surf. Winter is the best time of year for surfing here. Offshore winds are from the south southwest. Most of the surf here comes from groundswells and the ideal swell direction is from the north northeast.There is a left hand point break here. Likely to be crowded if working. Hazards include urchins, rips, rocks, locals and sharks.\" Wannasurf waiehu_beach_park: quality Regional Classic; experience All surfers; wave Reef-rocky, Right and left; swell size Starts working at  and holds up to; crowd weekday Crowded, weekend Ultra crowded; page has no GPS position. Other guide pins from this position: surf-forecast Waiehubeachpark 2.5 km."
