  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Honomanu Bay is a reef and point setup notched into the sea cliffs of northeast Maui, about twenty miles east of Ho'okipa on the Road to Hana. The main wave is a long, peeling left on the rocky western shore, which faces almost directly east and sits exposed to the tradewind. A shorter right breaks on the east side of the bay, more sheltered from that wind, though its quality leans heavily on swell direction. The bottom is a mix of lava, rock, and coral. Skill (surfnerd): Intermediate, Expert. Wannasurf honomanu_bay: quality World Class; experience Experienced surfers; wave Beach-break, Right and left; swell size Starts working at  and holds up to; crowd weekday Empty, weekend Few surfers. Access (surfnerd): Getting down to the parking lot depends on road conditions, which can be rough. Other guide pins from this position: wannasurf honomanu_bay 0.4 km. wannasurf pin 0.4 km from ours. surfnerd pin 0.0 km from ours. wannasurf good swell directions \"NorthWest, NorthEast\" are not one contiguous range."
