  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Hana Bay sits on the far eastern edge of Maui, in the town of Hana. A reef off each side of the bay shelters it from most swells, so it takes the right setup to break. When it does, a fun peak forms near the center of the beach in front of the rivermouth, peeling both right and left over a bottom of lava, rock, and coral. It rates below average overall, but has its worthwhile windows. Skill (surfnerd): Beginner, Intermediate, Expert. Access (surfnerd): Getting out is easy, with a short paddle from just about anywhere in the bay, and Hana Beach Park sits on the southern end. Keep an eye on the reef, and note that currents can keep you paddling to hold your position in the lineup. surfnerd pin 0.0 km from ours."
