  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Ma'alaea is one of Hawai'i's most famous summer spots, a right-hander that peels off a harbour breakwall and is widely considered the fastest wave in the world. It breaks over an uneven reef. Local activists and environmental groups have repeatedly blocked proposed extensions of the Ma'alaea jetty that would destroy this world-class wave. Surfnerd lists this break twice (maalaea-bay, maalaea-harbor); merged, same facing. Second Surfnerd entry https://www.surfnerd.com/surf-forecast/maalaea-harbor: workable swell SSE - SW , offshore None, 4ft - 7ft, Lava, Rock, Coral, Jetty, Reef, Point, Right, Low, Mid, High, Beginner, Intermediate, Expert, Spring, Summer, Autumn, Shortboard, Funboard, Longboard, Fish, Bodyboard, Kiteboard. Skill (surfnerd): Expert. Surf-forecast Maalaea: \"Ma'alaea in Maui is a fairly exposed reef break that has unreliable waves. Summer offers the optimum conditions for surfing. Works best in offshore winds from the north northwest. Tends to receive distant groundswells and the best swell direction is from the south. Left and better right hand reef breaks.. Best around mid tide. Sometimes crowded. Watch out for rocks/boats.\" Wannasurf maalaea: quality World Class; experience Experienced surfers; wave Reef-coral, Right; swell size Starts working at 1.0m-1.5m / 3ft-5ft and holds up to 4m+ / 12ft; crowd weekday Few surfers, weekend Crowded. Other guide pins from this position: surf-forecast Maalaea 0.5 km, wannasurf maalaea 0.3 km, surfnerd maalaea-harbor 0.2 km."
