  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: La Perouse Bay is a very rocky bay tucked into the desolate, beautiful southern corner of Maui, and it serves up powerful, clean lefts. The break sits over a mix of lava, rock, and coral in a pristine setting. On its day it delivers a long, workable left, though the shoulders can turn slopey and fat. Skill (surfnerd): Intermediate, Expert. Surf-forecast La-Perouse-Bay-The-Dumps: \"La Perouse Bay/The Dumps in Maui is a reasonably exposed reef break that only works once in a while. Summer offers the best conditions for surfing. Offshore winds are from the north northeast. Groundswells and windswells are equally likely and the best swell direction is from the south. A left hand reef break. Sometimes crowded. Watch out for rocks.\" Wannasurf la_perouse_bay: quality Normal; experience Experienced surfers; wave Reef-rocky, Left; swell size Starts working at 1.5m-2m /5ft-6ft and holds up to 5m / 16 ft and over; crowd weekday Empty, weekend Few surfers. Access (surfnerd): The road leads right down to the bay, though you may need a 4WD depending on current road conditions. Getting in and out over the rocky beach can be tricky, especially on a solid, consistent swell. Watch for shallow reef, strong currents, and the occasional shark sighting. Other guide pins from this position: surf-forecast La-Perouse-Bay-The-Dumps 1.6 km, wannasurf la_perouse_bay 0.3 km. wannasurf pin 0.3 km from ours. surfnerd pin 0.0 km from ours. surf-forecast pin 1.9 km from ours (its coordinates are given to 0.01°). surf-forecast: \"reasonably exposed reef\". Types differ (surfnerd Reef, Point; surf-forecast reasonably exposed reef); the non-beach type is recorded."
