  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Kaiolohia Bay, also known as Shipwreck Beach, is an 8-mile stretch of windswept coastline on the north side of Lanai, about a half-hour drive from Lanai City. It faces the Kalohi Channel, the shallow, 10-mile band of sea separating Lanai and Molokai. The sheer scale of the place means plenty of reefs to choose from, all breaking roughly 500 to 600 yards offshore over lava, rock, and coral. It stays pristine and largely empty, and the peaks throw both rights and lefts. Skill (surfnerd): Beginner, Intermediate, Expert. Access (surfnerd): Getting here means dirt roads only, so a 4x4 is a must. surfnerd pin 0.0 km from ours."
