  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Hideaways is a cluster of scattered reefbreaks tucked further east in Princeville, sitting at the base of high cliffs. It breaks over uneven reef and peels both left and right, holding fun waves when the surf is small and the wind stays down. It has had a shark attack, so it's worth keeping in the back of your mind. Check: surfnerd states facing NW but best swell NE (90 degrees apart); both are as published. Skill (surfnerd): Beginner. Surf-forecast Hideaways: \"Hideaways in Kauai is an exposed reef break that has fairly consistent surf. Winter is the favoured time of year for surfing here. The best wind direction is from the south southeast. Tends to receive distant groundswells and the ideal swell direction is from the north. A reef breaks right. When the surf is up, crowds are likely Beware of locals and sharks.\" Access (surfnerd): There's a car park with free parking, along with roadside parking nearby. Other guide pins from this position: surf-forecast Hideaways 0.6 km."
