  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Tunnels is a right-hand reef break on Kauai's North Shore, near Ha'ena where the road ends at the start of the Na Pali Coast. It breaks over live coral a long way from shore, so the paddle out is long rather than hard. As a point break, the longer the ride, the longer the paddle back. It's one of the best waves on the island and offers a barreling right when it's on. Skill (surfnerd): Expert. Surf-forecast Tunnels: \"Tunnels in Kauai is an exposed reef break that has reliable surf. Winter is the best time of year for surfing here. The best wind direction is from the south southeast. Tends to receive distant groundswells and the optimum swell angle is from the north. There are left and right breaking reefs. Surfable at all stages of the tide. It's sometimes crowded here. Beware of rips, sharks and rocks.\" Wannasurf tunnels: quality World Class; experience Experienced surfers; wave None, None; swell size Starts working at 1.0m-1.5m / 3ft-5ft and holds up to 3m+ / 10ft+; crowd weekday Few surfers, weekend Few surfers. Access (surfnerd): Getting in is easy: paddle out from anywhere along the sandy beach in the bay. There's free parking, including roadside spots. Other guide pins from this position: surf-forecast Tunnels 0.0 km, wannasurf tunnels 0.2 km."
