  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Kealia is a golden sand bay north of Kapaa, where the Kuhio Hwy skirts the shore. The waves break over uneven reef and sand, and the bay is usually a mess of onshore peaks that churn up the sand. Lefts tend to dominate on north swells and rights on south swells, with rip channels separating the peaks. Check: surfnerd states facing ESE but best swell NE (67.5 degrees apart); both are as published. Skill (surfnerd): Beginner. Surf-forecast Kealia: \"Kealia in Kauai is an exposed beach and reef break that has reasonably consistent surf and can work at any time of the year. The best wind direction is from the west southwest. Windswells and groundswells in equal measure and the best swell direction is from the northeast. The beach breaks offer lefts and rights and in addition there are both left and right reef breaks.. Surfable at all stages of the tide. It's often crowded here. Beware of rips and rocks.\" Wannasurf kealia: quality Regional Classic; experience Experienced surfers; wave Point-break, Right and left; swell size Starts working at Less than 1m / 3ft and holds up to 5m / 16 ft and over; crowd weekday Few surfers, weekend Crowded. Access (surfnerd): There's a car park with free parking, along with roadside parking nearby. Other guide pins from this position: surf-forecast Kealia 0.4 km, wannasurf kealia 0.4 km. Surfnerd's workable swell (S to NW, best NE (surfnerd)) has nothing within 60° of the ESE facing while its own exposure range contains the facing; the two disagree, so the workable range is not used. wannasurf pin 0.4 km from ours. surfnerd pin 0.0 km from ours. surf-forecast pin 0.8 km from ours (its coordinates are given to 0.01°). surf-forecast: \"exposed beach and reef\". Types differ (surfnerd Beach; surf-forecast exposed beach and reef); the non-beach type is recorded."
