  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Horners is a fickle left that swings around the reef off the Kauai Sands Hotel in Wailua. It has been a surfing spot for centuries, though it sees less and less use these days. The wave breaks over a mix of uneven reef and sand, and it is often inconsequential when it does come to life. Check: surfnerd states facing SE but best swell N (135 degrees apart); both are as published. Skill (surfnerd): Intermediate. Surf-forecast Wailua-Horners: \"Wailua/Horners in Kauai is an exposed reef break that does not work very often. Winter is the best time of year for surfing here. Offshore winds blow from the west southwest. Most of the surf here comes from groundswells and the optimum swell angle is from the north. There is a left hand reef break. Likely to be crowded if working. Take care of rips and rocks.\" Wannasurf horners: quality Normal; experience All surfers; wave Beach-break, Right and left; swell size Starts working at Less than 1m / 3ft and holds up to 4m+ / 12ft; crowd weekday Few surfers, weekend Crowded; page has no GPS position. Other guide pins from this position: surf-forecast Wailua-Horners 0.3 km."
