  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Kalapaki is a gentle, forgiving break tucked deep inside Nawiliwili Bay, with the Marriott sitting right on the beach. Waves peel both left and right over a mix of uneven reef and sand, which makes it an easy-going place for beginners and longboarders to get in the water. Skill (surfnerd): Beginner. Surf-forecast Kalapaki-Beach: \"Kalapaki Beach in Kauai is an exposed reef break that has quite reliable surf. Summer offers the optimum conditions for surfing. Offshore winds blow from the northwest. Waves just as likely from local windswells as from distant groundswells and the ideal swell direction is from the south southeast. A choice of left and right reefs. Often Crowded. Take care of rocks in the line up.\" Wannasurf kalapaki_beach: quality Normal; experience All surfers; wave None, None; swell size Starts working at  and holds up to; crowd weekday None, weekend Webcam url. Access (surfnerd): A surf school operates at the beach, and parking is easy with both free parking and roadside spots nearby. Other guide pins from this position: surf-forecast Kalapaki-Beach 0.4 km, wannasurf kalapaki_beach 0.1 km."
