  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: PK's, short for Prince Kuhio Condos and named after the 19th-century Hawaiian surfing pioneer, is a coral-and-lava reef that peels both left and right. The wave starts outside with an approachable take-off, then travels and reforms on its way to an inside right that breaks close to the seawall. Check: surfnerd states facing SSW but best swell SE (67.5 degrees apart); both are as published. Skill (surfnerd): Intermediate. Surf-forecast P-Ks: \"PKs in Kauai is an exposed reef break that has fairly consistent surf. Summer offers the best conditions for surfing. Offshore winds are from the north northeast. Tends to receive a mix of groundswells and windswells and the best swell direction is from the south. The reef provides both left and right breaks. Surfable at all stages of the tide. It's sometimes crowded here. Take care of urchins, rips and rocks.\" Wannasurf pks: quality Regional Classic; experience All surfers; wave Reef-rocky, Right and left; swell size Starts working at  and holds up to; crowd weekday Few surfers, weekend Few surfers. Access (surfnerd): There is a car park at the spot, plus restrooms and showers on hand. Other guide pins from this position: surf-forecast P-Ks 0.8 km, wannasurf pks 0.5 km."
