  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Brenneckes is a beach break on Kauai's Poipu coast, throwing up lefts and rights over a mix of uneven reef and sand. The tight cove holds punchy peaks, but it's a bodyboarding-only spot, so anyone hoping to stand up should look at the neighboring Poipu Beach breaks instead. Inside Waiohai is a sucky peak that comes alive on higher tide, while First Break serves up outside reef action best left to experts. Beginners can slide over to Lemon Drops for rolling walls over rock and sand. Skill (surfnerd): Beginner. Surf-forecast Brenneckes: \"Brenneckes in Kauai is an exposed reef break that has reasonably consistent surf. Summer offers the best conditions for surfing. Offshore winds are from the north northeast. Waves just as likely from local windswells as from distant groundswells and the best swell direction is from the south. Both left and right reef breaks. Surfable at all stages of the tide. It's sometimes crowded here. Beware of urchins, rips and rocks.\" Other guide pins from this position: surf-forecast Brenneckes 1.2 km."
