  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Poipu Outer Reef is a heavy, expert-level reef break on Kauai's south shore, throwing a shallow left barrel alongside a longer, more sloped right. The bottom is a mix of rock, coral and lava sitting very shallow, so it demands respect and rewards experience. Mellower, more popular waves break closer to the beach at Lemon Drops and Waiohai, and heading west past Poipu you'll find PKs, Centers, Heroins and Acid Drop, each with its own mood but all carrying the same shallow-reef risk. Skill (surfnerd): Expert. Access (surfnerd): Paddle straight out to the outside reef from Kiahuna Beach, where there's also a parking lot. Be ready for a long paddle, and note that currents can get bad at times. surfnerd pin 0.0 km from ours."
