  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Polihale is a long, sweeping beachbreak with numerous setups strung out along the sand. The bottom is mostly sand with occasional reef sections, and the beach is so wide that peaks scatter up and down its length. Combo swells spread the fun across the whole stretch, so it pays to walk the sand and find a good peak. During larger swells, watch for shifty surf and strong currents. Surfnerd has 2 entries for this break with different stated facings (polihale-hawaii=WNW, polihale=NW); seaward uses the primary entry (polihale-hawaii), both kept. Second Surfnerd entry https://www.surfnerd.com/surf-forecast/polihale: workable swell S - N (Best from N), offshore None, 2ft - 8ft, Sand, Beach, Left, Right, Low, Mid, High, Intermediate. Skill (surfnerd): Beginner, Intermediate, Expert. Surf-forecast Polihale: \"Polihale in Kauai is an exposed beach break that has fairly consistent surf. Winter is the best time of year for surfing here. Offshore winds are from the southeast. Tends to receive distant groundswells and the ideal swell angle is from the northwest. The beach breaks offer lefts and rights. When it's working here, it can get crowded. Watch out for Strong rips.\" Wannasurf Polihale: quality Regional Classic; experience All surfers; wave Beach-break, Right and left; swell size Starts working at Less than 1m / 3ft and holds up to 4m+ / 12ft; crowd weekday Few surfers, weekend Few surfers. Access (surfnerd): Access is easy. Enter the beach anywhere off the road that runs through Polihale State Park, find a good peak, and paddle out. Other guide pins from this pos wannasurf page is 3.6 km from our pin (over 3 km); not used. surfnerd pin 0.0 km from ours. surf-forecast pin 1.3 km from ours (its coordinates are given to 0.01°). surf-forecast: \"exposed beach\". Types differ (surfnerd Beach, Reef; surf-forecast exposed beach); the non-beach type is recorded."
