  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Pinetrees is a reef break that serves up both left and right peaks over an uneven, rocky reef. It rarely turns on perfect, but it's a dependable spot for intermediate surfers after rideable walls rather than flawless ones. Skill (surfnerd): Intermediate. Surf-forecast Pine-Trees: \"Pine Trees in Big Island is a quite exposed reef break that has very consistent surf and works all around the year. The best wind direction is from the east. Clean groundswells prevail and the best swell direction is from the west northwest. Right and better left hand reef breaks.. Surfable at all stages of the tide. It's sometimes crowded here. Watch out for urchins, rips, rocks and locals.\" Wannasurf pine_trees: quality Regional Classic; experience Experienced surfers; wave Reef-rocky, Right; swell size Starts working at  and holds up to; crowd weekday Few surfers, weekend Crowded. Access (surfnerd): Getting in is easy, with a paved road leading straight to the spot. There's a car park with free parking plus roadside parking, and camping is available nearby. Other guide pins from this position: surf-forecast Pine-Trees 0.9 km, wannasurf pine_trees 0.1 km."
