  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Kiholo Bay is a scenic reef setup with a choice of waves, tucked into pristine landscape alongside the Four Seasons resort. The peak in the middle of the bay is the obvious draw and hard to miss, while a right-hand pointbreak sits at the north end and is easy to overlook. Everything breaks over uneven reef, with the middle peak offering both lefts and rights. Skill (surfnerd): Beginner. Surf-forecast Kiholo-Bay: \"Kiholo Bay in Big Island is a fairly exposed beach and point break that has consistent surf. Winter is the optimum time of year for surfing here. Works best in offshore winds from the east southeast. Clean groundswells prevail and the ideal swell angle is from the northwest. Waves at the beach break both left and right Sometimes crowded. Watch out for rips and sharks.\" Access (surfnerd): There's a car park with free parking, plus roadside parking nearby. Other guide pins from this position: surf-forecast Kiholo-Bay 0.4 km."
