  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Keawaiki Bay is a reef break that peels both left and right over an uneven fringe of coral and lava. Any west swell should reach that reef and open up quick barrel sections in both directions, making it a fun, playful set-up when the pieces line up. Skill (surfnerd): Intermediate. Surf-forecast Keawaiki-Bay: \"Keawaiki Bay in Big Island is a reasonably exposed beach and reef break that has reliable surf. Winter is the best time of year for surfing here. The best wind direction is from the east southeast. Groundswells are more common than windswells and the best swell direction is from the northwest. Reef breaks provide lefts and rights. Sometimes crowded. Beware of rips and sharks.\" Access (surfnerd): There is free roadside parking near the highway, but reaching the water takes some effort. Plan on a trek in from the road, or the walk along the Kings Highway Foot Trail. The pay-off is a nice beach to hang out on once you have made it down. Other guide pins from this position: surf-forecast Keawaiki-Bay 0.5 km. surfnerd pin 0.1 km from ours. surf-forecast pin 0.3 km from ours (its coordinates are given to 0.01°). surf-forecast: \"reasonably exposed beach and reef\"."
