  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Kolekole is a right and left dumping reef peak, shaped in part by the Kolekole Stream that feeds down from Akaka Falls. It breaks over a bottom of lava, rock, and coral, with boulders scattered underneath. Both the right and the left suit bodysurfing and bodyboarding more than surfing, though the spot still has its moments. A rivermouth flows out here, so quality drops off after heavy rain, but it is usually okay. Overall it rates as a below-average wave that saves its best days for the right setup. Skill (surfnerd): Intermediate, Expert. Surf-forecast Kolekole: \"Kolekole in Big Island is an exposed river break that has quite reliable surf. Winter is the best time of year for surfing here. The best wind direction is from the west southwest. Most of the surf here comes from groundswells and the ideal swell direction is from the east northeast. The quality of the surf isn't affected by the tide. When it's working here, it can get crowded. Beware of - Rips / undertow - Rocks - Man-made danger (buoys etc.) - Pollution - Sharks.\" Wannasurf Kolekole: quality Normal; experience All surfers; wave Rivermouth, Right and left; swell size Starts working at 1.0m-1.5m / 3ft-5ft and holds up to 5m / 16 ft and over; crowd weekday Empty, weekend Crowded. Access (surfnerd): Getting in is easy, though the road down to the beach park is steep, and it is only a short paddle out. Keep an eye on the currents, which can get strong at times, and watch for the reef and large boulders. Water quality can suffer after heavy rain. Other guide pins from this position: surf-forecast Kol"
