  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Honolii Point sits on the Big Island's east coast just north of Hilo, a reliable rivermouth break also known as Honoli'i Beach Park. It serves up lefts and rights that break over boulders, with a fun lefthander peeling off the point on the north side of the rivermouth. When a sizable swell lines up on a lower tide, the walls can turn hollow and powerful. Because it's a rivermouth, the bottom shifts as boulders move with the flow, and water quality dips after heavy rain, though it's usually fine. Skill (surfnerd): Intermediate. Surf-forecast Honolii-Beach-Park: \"Honolii Beach Park in Big Island is an exposed reef break that has very consistent surf. Winter is the best time of year for surfing here. Offshore winds are from the southwest. Clean groundswells prevail and the best swell direction is from the northeast. There are left and right breaking reefs. Surfable at all stages of the tide. It's often crowded here. Take care of rocks, locals and sharks.\" Wannasurf honolii: quality Regional Classic; experience All surfers; wave Rivermouth, Right and left; swell size Starts working at 1.0m-1.5m / 3ft-5ft and holds up to 4m+ / 12ft; crowd weekday Crowded, weekend Ultra crowded. Wannasurf honoli_i: quality Normal; experience Experienced surfers; wave Reef-coral, Right and left; swell size Starts working at Less than 1m / 3ft and holds up to 3m+ / 10ft+; crowd weekday Few surfers, weekend Crowded. Access (surfnerd): Getting in is easy, with a car park at Honoli'i Beach Park plus restrooms and showers. Other guide pins from this position: surf-forecast Honolii-Be"
