  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Pohoiki is a lava-reef spot with three separate bays, each offering a different wave over an uneven reef. The bottom is extremely sharp lava rock dotted with urchins, so it pays to avoid contact at all times. The three bays give you options. First Bay sits closest to the boat ramp, with a wave that suits all levels and warm water from nearby volcanic springs. Second Bay lies a little further out in slightly cooler water and throws a more hollow, faster wave for advanced surfers. Third Bay, around a small rocky outcrop to the south, is hollow and fast over shallow water, and can turn into a solid big-wave spot when a strong swell meets west-to-north wind. Check: surfnerd states facing SSE but best swell NE (112.5 degrees apart); both are as published. Skill (surfnerd): Intermediate. Surf-forecast Pohoiki: \"Pohoiki in Big Island is an exposed reef break that has pretty consitent surf and can work at any time of the year. Works best in offshore winds from the west northwest. Windswells and groundswells in equal measure and the ideal swell angle is from the east. Both left and right reef breaks. When it's working here, it can get crowded. Take care of urchins, rocks, locals and sharks.\" Wannasurf pohiki: quality Regional Classic; experience All surfers; wave Reef-rocky, Right and left; swell size Starts working at 1.0m-1.5m / 3ft-5ft and holds up to; crowd weekday Few surfers, weekend Crowded. Access (surfnerd): Getting in is easy, with parking at Isaac Hale Beach Park. Other guide pins from this position: surf-forecast Pohoiki 3.1 km, wannasurf pohiki 0.6 km"
