  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Keauhou Point is a left-hand point break that breaks over uneven reef, set along a remote stretch of coast with incredible scenery. Rivers of lava hit the coast here, which gives you a clue to what the bottom is like. Skill (surfnerd): Intermediate. Surf-forecast Keauhou-Point: \"Keauhou Point in Big Island is an exposed reef break that has consistent surf. Summer offers the best conditions for surfing. Works best in offshore winds from the northwest. Groundswells are more common than windswells and the best swell direction is from the south southeast. A left hand reef break. Even when there are waves, it's not likley to be crowded. Beware of rips, rocks and sharks.\" Access (surfnerd): Getting here takes some effort: register first with the Kilauea Visitor Center in Hawaii Volcanoes National Park, then hike about 7 miles down the Keauhou trail to the coast. Other guide pins from this position: surf-forecast Keauhou-Point 1.0 km."
