  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Popoia Island, also known as Flat Island, is a small four-acre isle sitting about a quarter-mile off Kailua Beach Park. The main wave is a left point that breaks over reef and wraps around the island on the best days, with a shorter right peeling off the other side. Both waves stay mellow, which makes Popoia a friendly place for beginners and longboarders. Skill (surfnerd): Beginner, Intermediate. Wannasurf Popoia_Island: quality Sloppy; experience All surfers; wave Reef-coral, Left; swell size Starts working at Less than 1m / 3ft and holds up to 2.5m+ / 8ft+; crowd weekday Empty, weekend Few surfers. Access (surfnerd): Getting here is easy enough, but there is a long paddle out to the island from Kailua Beach Park. Long rides also mean long paddles back, so pace yourself. Other guide pins from this position: wannasurf Popoia_Island 0.3 km. wannasurf pin 0.3 km from ours. surfnerd pin 0.0 km from ours."
