  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Dumps is a left-hand reef point on the remote Makena Coast, at the southern corner of Maui. It sits in pristine, desolate countryside and can turn really good when a sizable swell arrives. The wave breaks fast over a bottom of lava, rock, and coral, throwing up barrel sections on moderate to large swells. On smaller days it slows down and fattens out noticeably. Skill (surfnerd): Intermediate, Expert. Surf-forecast Dumps-1: \"Dumps in Maui is a fairly exposed reef break that does not work very often. Summer offers the best conditions for surfing. Offshore winds blow from the east northeast. Tends to receive a mix of groundswells and windswells and the best swell direction is from the south southwest. Even when the surf is up, crowds are unknown. Take care of - Urchins - Rocks.\" Wannasurf Dumps: quality Normal; experience Experienced surfers; wave Reef-coral, Left; swell size Starts working at Less than 1m / 3ft and holds up to 5m / 16 ft and over; crowd weekday Few surfers, weekend Few surfers. Access (surfnerd): You'll find Dumps just off Makena Road, with a big parking lot. Other guide pins from this position: surf-forecast Dumps-1 0.3 km, wannasurf Dumps 0.3 km."
