  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Little Beach, also known as Pu'u Ola'i Beach, sits on the southern end of Maui right next to Big Beach, a scenic cove that mostly serves up shorepound. Most days it is skimboarding, bodysurfing, and bodyboarding territory, with beach break that can turn sizeable and strong and throw closeout barrels. On bigger, longer-period swells a surfboard option can open up off the rocks on the sides of the cove. It is also the only generally accepted clothing-optional beach on Maui. Skill (surfnerd): Beginner, Intermediate, Expert. Surf-forecast Little-Beach-1: \"Little Beach in Maui is a quite exposed reef break that only works once in a while. Summer offers the best conditions for surfing. Ideal winds are from the east northeast. Waves just as likely from local windswells as from distant groundswells and the optimum swell angle is from the south southwest. Often Crowded. Take care of - Urchins - Rips / undertow - Rocks - Localism - Sharks.\" Wannasurf little_beach: quality Normal; experience Experienced surfers; wave Reef-coral, Right and left; swell size Starts working at 1.0m-1.5m / 3ft-5ft and holds up to 5m / 16 ft and over; crowd weekday Crowded, weekend Ultra crowded. Access (surfnerd): Getting in is easy, off Makena Road at Makena State Park. Other guide pins from this position: surf-forecast Little-Beach-1 0.1 km, wannasurf little_beach 0.1 km."
