  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Shark Pit is a shallow reef break near Lahaina that peels both left and right over uneven reef. The name is a warning worth heeding, so stay vigilant in the water. This one is strictly for expert surfers. Skill (surfnerd): Expert. Surf-forecast Shark-Pit: \"Shark Pit in Maui is a fairly exposed reef break that has reasonably consistent surf and can work at any time of the year. The best wind direction is from the northeast. Most of the surf here comes from groundswells and the best swell direction is from the west southwest. Both left and right reef breaks. Best around mid tide. When the surf is up, it can get quite busy in the water. Take care of rocks,urchins and sharks.\" Wannasurf sharkpit: quality Totally Epic; experience Experienced surfers; wave Reef-coral, Right and left; swell size Starts working at 1.0m-1.5m / 3ft-5ft and holds up to 4m+ / 12ft; crowd weekday Few surfers, weekend Crowded; page has no GPS position. Access (surfnerd): You'll find free roadside parking nearby. Other guide pins from this position: surf-forecast Shark-Pit 0.9 km."
