  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: The Cove is a mellow, slow-rolling left at the southern end of Kalama Park, fronting Cove Park, and one of the best places to learn to surf on Maui. The wave peels over a reef of lava, rock and coral, and it stays user-friendly even though the overall rating sits on the modest side. It's usually small and packed with surf schools, but it can genuinely turn on when a bigger swell arrives. Skill (surfnerd): Beginner, Intermediate, Expert. Surf-forecast Kihei-Cove: \"Kihei Cove in Maui is a fairly exposed reef break that is often working. Summer offers the best conditions for surfing. The best wind direction is from the northeast. Clean groundswells prevail and the ideal swell angle is from the west southwest. Good surf at all stages of the tide. When the surf is up, crowds are likely Hazards include urchins and rocks.\" Wannasurf kihei_cove: quality Normal; experience Beginners wave; wave Reef-rocky, Right and left; swell size Starts working at Less than 1m / 3ft and holds up to 2m+ / 6ft+; crowd weekday Crowded, weekend Ultra crowded. Access (surfnerd): Getting in is easy: paddle out from anywhere along Kalama Beach Park or Cove Beach Park. The main thing to watch for is the reef underneath. Other guide pins from this position: surf-forecast Kihei-Cove 0.3 km, wannasurf kihei_cove 0.3 km."
