  "notes": "Surfnerd overview: Infinities serves up long, near-perfect lefts tucked into the southwest corner at Pakala. It's a point break peeling over an uneven reef, and it comes into its own on the bigger summer south swells. Check: surfnerd states facing WSW but best swell SE (112.5 degrees apart); both are as published. Skill (surfnerd): Intermediate. Surf-forecast Infinities_1: \"Infinities in Kauai is an exposed reef and point break that has pretty consitent surf and can work at any time of the year. The best wind direction is from the northeast. Clean groundswells prevail and the best swell direction is from the south.There is a left breaking point here. When the surf is up, it can get quite busy in the water. Take care of the strong rips here.\" Access (surfnerd): There's a car park at the spot. Other guide pins from this position: surf-forecast Infinities_1 0.3 km."
